WEBVTT

00:00:00.007 --> 00:00:01.962
Here is the path we’ll follow.

00:00:01.962 --> 00:00:07.242
We begin with variables, because variables give names to values.

00:00:07.242 --> 00:00:15.377
Then we look at data types so Python can distinguish numbers, text, and True or False values.

00:00:15.377 --> 00:00:24.732
Next, we use arithmetic to create useful metrics, then we format results so they are easier for people to read.

00:00:24.732 --> 00:00:32.757
We also look at type conversion because data often arrives as text even when we eventually want to calculate with it.

00:00:33.207 --> 00:00:36.714
Everything builds toward a small sales calculator.

00:00:36.714 --> 00:00:44.444
If you can follow how a value moves from raw input to calculation and finally to readable output,

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.963
you have the main idea of this module.
